 "title": "Dual bidirectional TVS for CAN bus lines, 24 V working voltage, SOT-23",
 "source": {
  "document": "NUP2105L/D",
  "revision": "Rev. 5, January 2012",
  "pages": 7
 },
 "summary": "NUP2105L is a pair of bidirectional transient voltage suppressors in one SOT-23, made to sit across the CAN_H and CAN_L lines of a CAN node and shunt ESD, fast transients and surges to ground. Each line stands off 24 V, breaks down between 26.2 V and 32 V, and clamps at 44 V max with 8 A of 8 × 20 µs surge, rated 350 W peak per line. Capacitance is 30 pF max per line to ground, and leakage 100 nA max at 24 V. The part is AEC-Q101 qualified and PPAP capable; the SZ prefix is for automotive and other applications with unique site and control change requirements.",
